Replace the synchronous `verimark_enroll` (with its inline 12-opcode
prelude, multi-swipe loop, and dual-timer RICH↔SPARSE keep-alive /
poll cadence that all blocked the libfprint GMainLoop) with an
`fpi_ssm` carrying 43 states.

Architecture :
- Setup (3 ops) : `ENR_S_GEN_TUID` (host random nonce) →
  `ENR_S_PRE_GETLIST` (0x9f pre-snapshot for the post-commit tuid
  diff) → `ENR_S_PRE_INIT_0X19`.
- PRELUDE (12 ops, all tolerant — match the sync code's best-effort
  semantics) : events / 0x39 RICH / 0x80 verify-style / 0x39 SPARSE /
  0x81 / 0x99 verify probe / 0x39 ENROLL_E mode-switch.
- `ENR_S_BEGIN` : 0x96 01 (strict, fails on transport error).
- Per-swipe loop : drain (6 ops, cursor_a/b advance per
  `useful_swipes`) → 0x39 WARM → 0x39 ENROLL_D|RICH → 0x86 arm →
  0x80 ENROLL → poll cycle → teardown (3 ops) → 0x96 02 add_image →
  decision (loop or commit).
- **Single-timer polling** : one `g_timeout_add` 250 ms +
  dispatcher state (`ENR_S_SWIPE_POLL_DISPATCH`) that picks
  deadline / keep-alive / read at each tick. Cleaner than the
  two-concurrent-timer pattern envisaged in the roadmap. Keep-alive
  0x39 SPARSE↔RICH every 500 ms — without it the firmware disarms
  the FSM and the LED goes dark mid-swipe.
- Verdict parsing (0x96 02 response) : `verdict_char` (0x64 =
  accepted) + bitmask @ 0x14/0x15 LE. Bitmask-advance →
  `fpi_device_enroll_progress`. Bitmask 0x7f → commit.
- Commit (123-byte payload) + 0x9e 01 db_refresh + 0x96 04 finish
  + 0x9f post-snapshot + diff pre/post lists to resolve the
  device-reassigned storage_handle (some sensors don't honour the
  host-supplied tuid).
- Failure path consolidated via `ENR_S_CLEANUP_FINISH` :
  best-effort 0x96 04 then `mark_failed` with `ctx->fatal_error`.
  Same invariant as the sync code (3-consecutive-timeout fail,
  bitmask < 0x7f fail, commit refused fail).

Removed dead code now that all four heavy vfuncs (open / verify /
identify / enroll) bypass the sync vtable :
- `verimark_enroll_drain_pre_cycle` (60 LOC)
- `verimark_enroll_one_swipe`        (110 LOC)
- `verimark_enroll_prelude`          (40 LOC)
- inline orchestrator                (200 LOC)
- `verimark_io_bind` + forward decl  (15 LOC)

`verimark_enroll` itself becomes a 5-line trampoline calling
`verimark_run_enroll_ssm`.

GCancellable from `fpi_device_get_cancellable()` is wired into
every async opcode → Ctrl+C / EnrollStop now propagate cleanly,
matching the verify/identify improvement landed in Phase 10.3.d.

Builds clean (zero warnings) against libfprint 1.94.10 / libgusb
0.4.9 / GLib 2.86 on NixOS. 11 standalone TDD suites stay green —
the SSM lives in `verimark.c` gated behind `VERIMARK_HAVE_LIBGUSB`,
invisible to the standalone build.

Runtime validation via `fprintd-enroll $(whoami)` against the real
sensor pending — risk-graded high since this is the largest single
vfunc orchestration in the driver.

AI-assisted.
